374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (     However, one does not have to walk far to find that these land use patterns are rather limited in their geographic extent. If a visitor walks just a few blocks away from the station in any direction, they will quickly encounter single-family homes, wide roads such as Commerce Drive and Clairemont Avenue, and gas stations and surface parking lots. However, Downtown Decatur is not the only area in the city where it is possible to find walkable neighborhoods and denser housing. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
